 ### Requirement: Trunk-tip revision pinned at launch
 
-In the operator-agent mode, a run started without `--revision` whose clone's HEAD is a revision that an in-force observation consent names, whatever that consent's subject identity and whichever act made it, SHALL pin that HEAD exactly as REQ-polaris-generation-033 states, and this requirement changes nothing else for it. Every other run SHALL pin exactly one revision at launch, before the question of REQ-polaris-generation-046 is asked, and that revision SHALL NOT change within the run. Absent `--revision`, it SHALL be the commit the repository's trunk points to in the operator's clone: the branch the clone records as its remote's default (the remote's `HEAD` reference), or, where it records none, the clone's `main` branch, or, where there is none, its `master` branch. Where none of these exists, Syzygy SHALL refuse, naming `--revision`. With `--revision`, the pinned revision SHALL be the commit the operator names, given as a full or unambiguous abbreviated object identifier or a reference the clone holds, resolved once to a full object identifier; a name that resolves to no commit, or to more than one, SHALL be refused.
+In the operator-agent mode, a run started without `--revision` whose clone's HEAD is a revision that an in-force observation consent names, whatever that consent's subject identity and whichever act made it, SHALL pin that HEAD exactly as REQ-polaris-generation-033 states, and this requirement changes nothing else for it. Every other run SHALL pin exactly one revision at launch, before the question of REQ-polaris-generation-046 is asked, and that revision SHALL NOT change within the run. Absent `--revision`, it SHALL be the commit the repository's trunk points to in the operator's clone: the branch the clone records as its remote's default (the remote's `HEAD` reference), or, where it records none, the clone's `main` branch, or, where there is none, its `master` branch. Where none of these exists, Syzygy SHALL refuse, naming `--revision`. The remote's default is the commit that the remote-tracking branch named by the symbolic reference `refs/remotes/<remote>/HEAD` points to, where the remote is `origin` when it records one, or else the one remote that records one; where several remotes record one and none is `origin`, the clone records no single remote default, and Syzygy SHALL refuse, naming `--revision`. `main` and `master` are the local branches `refs/heads/main` and `refs/heads/master`. While a remote default is recorded, no local branch is consulted for the pin: where a local branch of the same name points elsewhere, the launch output SHALL state both identifiers and that a local commit is not the trunk default. With `--revision`, the pinned revision SHALL be the commit the operator names, given as a full or unambiguous abbreviated object identifier or a reference the clone holds, resolved once to a full object identifier; a name that resolves to no commit, or to more than one, SHALL be refused. An abbreviated identifier resolves to more than one when more than one object identifier the clone stores begins with it, decided from the loose object file names and the pack indexes alone, without reading those objects. A reference that names an object other than a commit, an annotated tag included, SHALL be refused, naming `--revision`, after Syzygy reads at most that one object's type, and SHALL NOT be followed to the object it names.
 
 Syzygy SHALL make no network request to choose or verify the revision: the trunk tip is the one the operator's clone holds at launch, and whether it is the upstream's latest commit is Inferred. The launch output and the run record SHALL state the pinned revision in full, the reference it came from, the commit's committer date as the commit object records it, and that Syzygy did not fetch; they SHALL print the operator's own command to update the clone before a later run.
 
-Syzygy SHALL NOT change the clone's checkout. Where the clone's HEAD is not the pinned revision, Syzygy SHALL refuse before asking for consent, and SHALL print the one command that checks out the pinned revision, so that REQ-polaris-generation-033's HEAD check holds at the brief. The pinned revision is the revision the launch consent names; REQ-polaris-generation-033's rules for it apply unchanged.
+Syzygy SHALL NOT change the clone's checkout. HEAD may be detached or name a branch; only the commit it resolves to is compared with the pinned revision. Where the clone's HEAD is not the pinned revision, Syzygy SHALL refuse before asking for consent, and SHALL print the one command that checks out the pinned revision, so that REQ-polaris-generation-033's HEAD check holds at the brief, with the warning that a checkout carries uncommitted changes over. The pinned revision is the revision the launch consent names; REQ-polaris-generation-033's rules for it apply unchanged.
+
+For a launch-consented run, Syzygy SHALL accept the operator's clone in whatever form holds the pinned revision: a full clone with its history, branches, tags, remote-tracking references, stash and reflogs, a clone made by fetching one commit alone, or any form between. It SHALL NOT refuse the clone for holding commits, objects or references beyond the pinned revision, and SHALL NOT fetch, prune, repack or otherwise change it. Whatever the clone holds, Syzygy's reads of it for the run are only these. The object reads are Git object reads by object identifier, as REQ-polaris-generation-033 and REQ-polaris-generation-046 state them. The reference, configuration and Git-directory reads are launch reads, not observer object reads: Syzygy makes them only to pin the revision, to compare HEAD with it and to propose the identity, and they read no repository content, so REQ-polaris-generation-033's object-read rule governs every read of content:
+
+- objects: the pinned commit object, its root tree and the trees and blobs reachable from it, reached by walking down from the commit, from the loose object files, the pack files and the pack indexes under `objects/`; Syzygy SHALL read no parent commit object and no object reached only from another commit, a branch, a tag, the stash, a reflog or a note, and SHALL use the pinned commit's parent identifiers only as REQ-polaris-generation-046 uses them, never resolving one;
+- pack storage: where a pack stores an object of that scope as a delta, Syzygy MAY read the stored bytes of the delta's base, whichever object they belong to, solely to reconstruct that object, which it then re-hashes as REQ-polaris-generation-033 requires; it SHALL NOT use a base reached this way for anything else, and SHALL NOT classify, store, quote, record a digest of, render or send it, and the launch output, the run record and every page SHALL state that objects of the pinned tree may have been rebuilt from delta bases outside it, whose stored bytes were inflated only for that and never read as content;
+- references: the names of the clone's references, and the values only of `HEAD` and the reference it names, the references the trunk rule above names, the local branch of the remote default's name, and the reference `--revision` names, each read as file data from the loose reference files and `packed-refs`; a clone that stores its references otherwise (the reftable backend) SHALL be refused before asking for consent, naming the reason;
