+- nothing else in the Git directory, and nothing in the working tree or the index. Syzygy SHALL NOT read either to learn whether the checkout holds uncommitted or untracked changes, and SHALL start no process that reads or acts on the clone, wherever that process runs (a Git command given the clone's Git directory from elsewhere included), so no hook or filter runs.
+
+A clone whose objects of that scope cannot be read without an alternate, a replacement object or a fetch, a partial clone missing one included, SHALL be refused as REQ-polaris-generation-033 states, and Syzygy SHALL NOT fetch the missing object. Because Syzygy reads no working tree, it cannot tell whether the checked-out files differ from the pinned revision, while the agent sessions read them: the launch output, the run record and every page SHALL state that the working tree was not inspected and may differ from the pinned revision, and the launch output SHALL print the operator's own command that lists such changes (`git -C <clone> status --short`). Every brief and packet Syzygy issues to an agent session of a launch-consented run, the authoring and the review sessions alike, SHALL tell that session to rest no claim on any commit but the pinned revision and not to read the clone's history or other references; that a session complied is its own report, labelled Inferred. This changes nothing for a run that relies on no launch consent record: whatever form its observation consent record states for the clone still binds that run.
 
